{:edb/db-before-t 2275 :edb/db-after-t 2276 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535588 50 #inst "2026-10-14T16:33:29.816Z" 13194139535588 17592186045417 true] [17592186167031 1050 540.0 13194139535588 17592186045417 true] [17592186168089 1064 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nWe can define the **reciprocal hyperbolic functions** similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions.\n\nThe **hyperbolic cosecant function** (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\csch{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sinh{x}} = \\dfrac{2}{e^x-e^{-x}}\\,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\csch x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/cc/cc0b2c19d1606c8a0a2c11411a0b0a4fbc09f264d9d28d0fcb2fb81f6c576a8a.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\csch x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x \\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- It is an odd function." 13194139535588 17592186045417 false] [17592186168089 1064 "We can define the **reciprocal hyperbolic functions** similarly to how we define reciprocal trigonometric functions. \n\nThe **hyperbolic cosecant function** (pronounced \"cosetch\") is defined as \n![](images/c1/c112c1732880af3a22ea3831581062f4b7d8a96ad3408e9a98af0387691e9af7.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/1d/1de5a1885eb15a44f9de1b9d170b8906f684c1784f5f67de840cca1628f2ec91.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/cc/cc0b2c19d1606c8a0a2c11411a0b0a4fbc09f264d9d28d0fcb2fb81f6c576a8a.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/ea/ea88889bed67f76a0de3b6f4d3acd48051d741d4c51b8013b69fd6642e30eac1.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/56/56c0f97156e3980b9cf25c7204e993714a0879ba463132c958267e5927e71f4c.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/e8/e8eea575c16295c549b3019751f3562aa98b9d6f3e15375c24837521528878ca.svg)\n\n- It has a vertical asymptote ![](images/29/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\n- It has a horizontal asymptote ![](images/6c/6c63827e94b6c11a9803605bd54156d90d3fcc6ff4639dd179a5fb024bcffaa1.svg)\n\n- It is an odd function." 13194139535588 17592186045417 true] [17592186168105 1064 "$$\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits} \\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}\n$$\n\nThe **hyperbolic secant function** (pronounced \"sesh\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\sech{x} = \\dfrac{1}{\\cosh{x}} = \\dfrac{2}{e^x+e^{-x}}\\,\\,\\,\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\sech x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b228f9fba9d1b981d64730de4b3836de914e2565332780a3fd803c165fb7d2ba.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\sech x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x \\in (-\\infty, \\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (0, 1]$.\n- It has the horizontal asymptote $y=0$.\n- It is an even function." 13194139535588 17592186045417 false] [17592186168105 1064 "The **hyperbolic secant function** (pronounced \"sesh\") is defined as \n![](images/e7/e7c30afe931272f96d3af0ae8b020cd011c0d3a16bc299bf6afb58a3853d5923.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/b6/b63b49cef7052e7402e9f894d46b94ffb2f406b51d57402272dba5aade93a508.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/b2/b228f9fba9d1b981d64730de4b3836de914e2565332780a3fd803c165fb7d2ba.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/e8/e82bcae39f329ede047f75bb74921d7a2a9d55f74b529a98fee4581b87d35849.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/aa/aa2627839a0a228b0c54166eb26bf5943e21bbb690d71d1059b5bad6f36d72bd.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/70/70c4b1eec58c8b8a94bc35b936d5d3ce5ea71f302517d16eb81e3fa7adf7afec.svg)\n\n- It has a horizontal asymptote ![](images/6c/6c63827e94b6c11a9803605bd54156d90d3fcc6ff4639dd179a5fb024bcffaa1.svg)\n\n- It is an even function." 13194139535588 17592186045417 true] [17592186168106 1064 "The **hyperbolic cotangent function** (pronounced \"coth\") is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\coth x = \\frac{1}{\\tanh x} &= \\frac{e^{x} + e^{-x}}{e^{x} - e^{-x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=\\coth x$ is shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d3d4f5cbe846f7725399fa1b1769c4f476be439575043537a2caa80c318a5ec9.png)\n\nNote the following properties of $y=\\coth x$:\n\n- Its domain is $x\\in (-\\infty, 0)\\cup (0,\\infty)$.\n- Its range is $y \\in (-\\infty, -1)\\cup (1,\\infty)$.\n- It has horizontal asymptotes $y=\\pm 1$.\n- It is an odd function.\n\nUsing the alternative definitions of $\\tanh x$, we can write down two more definitions for $\\coth x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\coth x &= \\frac{1}{\\tanh x} \\\\\n&= \\frac{e^{2x} + 1}{e^{2x} - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1 + e^{-2x}}{1 - e^{-2x}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535588 17592186045417 false] [17592186168106 1064 "The **hyperbolic cotangent function** (pronounced \"coth\") is defined as \n![](images/a7/a76c7780cd40b24bf3cb5dcd55eecd4c14e4a79825cba1501d4b8afd425405ba.svg)\nThe graph of ![](images/15/158841441ef667264704ceb47ea5e26bac1385fef070fd7e42ae1527bada9631.svg) is shown below.\n\n![](images/d3/d3d4f5cbe846f7725399fa1b1769c4f476be439575043537a2caa80c318a5ec9.png)\n\nNote the following properties of ![](images/d9/d90a56456cf17cffd5fe59547103b45ba1ba186c40060f43e3674e66fcd69434.svg)\n\n- Its domain is ![](images/56/56c0f97156e3980b9cf25c7204e993714a0879ba463132c958267e5927e71f4c.svg)\n\n- Its range is ![](images/f1/f111c1f23a40b18e1e4baf575183e31bcc8d7987e90a8a16e024c252b61699d3.svg)\n\n- It has a vertical asymptote ![](images/29/29da0a4605613d6a7fd9e7bb2f4fb45cbabe8a47109971682844cb222486a20c.svg)\n\n- It has horizontal asymptotes ![](images/84/849544fed9b7437b1c0d262b2cf17d4539f767beab6ba7c8a7de82cff4c7ca68.svg)\n\n- It is an odd function.\n\nUsing the alternative definitions of ![](images/0d/0d5fcc991aa44ea723f4c42355e8a876b33441902dfb72ae82d4917ffff1b16b.svg) we can write down two more definitions for ![](images/94/944a08f36feb5caee9da43f160c130a4b48b46f5f28fe5be3147a272b600eb74.svg)\n![](images/d2/d26afd4eb7797e35fab8b46d018a646cf1faf02c7ffae9311587754ed210ef31.svg)" 13194139535588 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {} :edb/committed false :edb/speculative true}
